hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-14 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #5279 , toNat #5737) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-15 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-15 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #5737 , toNat #6055) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-16 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-16 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #6055 , toNat #6416) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-17 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-17 = unlines (cons "None of the six limits of today's knowledge graphs (the edge a bare assertion, identity by declaration, inference outside the graph, uncertainty a number, the schema outside the data, embeddings and retrieval that drop structure) is an engineering lapse. Each comes from the primitive: an edge that is an assertion, not a" (cons "construction." nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-18 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-18 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #6537 , toNat #6606) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-19 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-19 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #6606 , toNat #7143) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-20 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-20 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "An edge, like a node, is also an object of the store addressed by content, and its type is the relation it establishes. The paper's elementary form (§1 " (cons "The" nil))) (cons (quoted (cons "universe and its descriptions" (cons ", " (cons "Routines, relations, and rationales" (cons ", equation 1.5) is that a requirement on a" nil))))) (cons "function is a chosen dependent family P, and the reasoning that establishes it is a term" (cons "" (cons "  q : Π_{a:A} P(a, f(a))." (cons "" (cons "Read as a knowledge graph, the relation is the type and the edge is the term. An edge that inhabits its type is its" (cons "justification. There's no separate provenance layer, because the provenance is the term's content: whatever" (cons "premises it uses appear in it as references to other objects, by content. Asking why an edge holds means reading" (cons "the edge." nil))))))))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-21 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-21 = unlines (cons "That an edge is a term inhabiting the type of the relation it establishes changes what composition means. Combining two facts in an RDF graph means putting their triples in one set." (cons "Combining two constructions means applying one to the other. The result has a type that says exactly what was" (cons "established and a body that says exactly how. Composition of knowledge is composition of code, and its correctness" (cons "is checked." nil))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-22 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-22 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #8182 , toNat #8242) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-23 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-23 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #8242 , toNat #8751) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-24 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-24 = unlines (cons "**Identity has a witness.** To say two descriptions are the same thing is to give the equivalence e : A ≃ B whose path ua(e) transports what depends on them. The witness is" (cons "an object in the graph, open to inspection and reuse, and it says exactly what corresponds to what." nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-25 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-25 = unlines (cons "**What crosses an identity is determined.** Transport carries exactly what depends on the carrier through the" (cons "stated structure, and nothing else. The failure mode Halpin documented (owl:sameAs links that assert only similarity or relatedness, across which every property crosses anyway) can't arise. A weaker relation (a" (cons "projection that forgets information, a refinement, a correspondence in some respects) has a different type, and it" (cons "supports exactly the transfers its type licenses. The paper says this directly: an observation that forgets" (cons "information, a refinement of behavior, and an equivalence of complete structures have different types and" (cons (quoted (cons "consequences, and calling two things " (cons "the same" (cons " supplies none of the evidence." nil)))) nil))))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-26 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-26 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #9590 , toNat #10208) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-27 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-27 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #10208 , toNat #10266) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-28 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-28 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #10266 , toNat #10751) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-29 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-29 = unlines (cons "The fiber of histories compatible with a reading, and the warrant over that whole fiber, is how a knowledge graph should represent incomplete knowledge. A source that reports something is an" (cons "observation. What follows from the report is whatever holds for every state of affairs compatible with it. Missing" (cons "information is kept as the family of possibilities, not compressed into a number. Combining two sources intersects" (cons "their fibers, and refining an observation shrinks the fiber, so a conclusion established on the coarser fiber stays" (cons "established on the finer one. When a probability structure really is given, it is extra information that further" (cons "reasoning can use. It isn't a stand-in for the information that's absent." nil))))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-30 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-30 = unlines (cons "Representing incomplete knowledge as warrants over fibers settles the open-world versus closed-world split that divided the semantic web from databases. Open-world" (cons "reasoning says absence of a fact isn't its negation. Closed-world reasoning says it is. In hyperactivity, absence is" (cons (quoted (cons "itself an observation with a fiber. A dependency certificate (§10.5 " (cons "Dependency certificates and persistent" nil))) (cons (quoted (cons "evaluation" (cons ") records a lookup that found nothing as a dependency on that absence at a given revision. So a" nil))) (cons "conclusion drawn from absence is valid exactly while the absence holds, and the graph knows when it stops holding." nil)))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-31 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-31 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "The fiber construction that governs what a reading warrants also governs action (§10.4 " (cons "Observations, information, and locally available actions" (cons ", equation" nil)))) (cons "10.11). An action is safe at an observation when its condition holds over every compatible state:" (cons "" (cons "  SafeAt(y) := Π_{(s,p):Fiber_o(y)} P(s)." (cons "" (cons "A knowledge graph that drives decisions (in an organization, an agent or an instrument) needs exactly this: the" (cons "evidence that a decision is justified by what is actually known, not by a guess about the hidden state." nil)))))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-32 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-32 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #12426 , toNat #12486) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-33 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-33 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #12486 , toNat #12667) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-34 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-34 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #12667 , toNat #13180) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-35 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-35 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #13180 , toNat #13690) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-36 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-36 = unlines (cons "Two smaller consequences follow from objects kept by content and derived results kept with their certificates. Versioning is free: a changed fact is a new object with a new key, and the old one" (cons "stays; the history of a fact is the sequence of bindings of its name to keys. Reproducibility is by content: a" (cons "conclusion names, by content, exactly the premises it was drawn from." nil)))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-37 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-37 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #13988 , toNat #14065) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-38 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-38 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #14065 , toNat #14653) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-39 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-39 = unlines (cons "That the ontology, the constraint language, the query language and the reasoner are objects inside the graph means, for knowledge graphs, that a schema is a value in the graph, and evolving the schema is a construction over" (cons "that value. Migrating data across a schema change is transport along the relation between the old schema and the" (cons "new one. A query is a function over the graph's values, and its result can be kept as a maintained view with a" (cons "certificate. A reasoning rule is a construction, and its applications are terms that cite it. Nothing about the" (cons "graph's semantics is outside the graph." nil)))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-40 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-40 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #15143 , toNat #15209) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-41 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-41 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #15209 , toNat #15933) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-42 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-42 = unlines (cons "That an expression's meaning depends on who receives it, with what history, under which interpretation, means three things for knowledge graphs. A statement is an event: its source, its time and the context it" (cons "answered are part of it, and extraction keeps the event and builds what it warrants as a construction over it." (cons "Disagreement between sources is information, not noise: two sources whose statements conflict are two" (cons "observations, and the fiber compatible with both says what the conflict leaves open. The provenance of human" (cons "knowledge becomes first-class: a person's words, kept whole and addressed by content, are the inputs, and what the" (cons "graph concludes from them is a construction that cites them." nil))))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-43 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-43 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #16543 , toNat #16583) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-44 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-44 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #16583 , toNat #17420) nil))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-45 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-45 = unlines (cons "That the workflow graph and the knowledge graph are one graph closes the loop current systems leave open. A knowledge graph should know what its knowledge is for, which" (cons "questions it was assembled to answer, and which conclusions are still missing. In hyperactivity, purposes are" (cons "nodes, evidence is objects, and the paths from evidence to purpose are constructions. On 2026-11-15, organizing" (cons "about 50 knowledge-work targets and what they rest on needed no new primitive: the task graph, documents by content" (cons "(lib/document.cub) and projections of one value (lib/paper.cub) already were the system." nil)))))
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-46 : List Word
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-46 = mask-select hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source (ranges-mask (cons (toNat #17960 , toNat #17981) nil))
